---
alwaysApply: true
---
Random number generator (RNG) reproducibility rules:

- use `seed_random()` from `src/model/config.py` for global seeding
- do NOT call `np.random.seed()` directly outside `seed_random()`
- do NOT introduce new nondeterminism (time-based seeds, unordered iteration, etc.)

For new code:
- accept an optional `rng` parameter (numpy Generator) for explicit control
- default to global RNG behavior to preserve existing tests
- document which functions depend on random state

Existing contract:
- `seed_random()` sets global NumPy RNG; tests rely on this
- same seed must produce same results across runs
